## Mission

Add the package-specific contract between static/semantic analysis and any authorized disposable-VM run. The repository already proves VM-lane readiness; this PR makes one package's trust, decoding, authorization, guest-isolation, acceptance, evidence, and rollback gates explicit before a VM or installer can start.

## Delivered

- closed Draft 2020-12 package VM qualification profile schema;
- read-only harness operation contract;
- dependency-free fail-closed profile validator;
- sanitized blocked Allscripts profile with no real package, signer, endpoint, hostname, argument, or approval;
- explicit blockers for offline trust, approved package-family trust policy, online revocation, strong-name verification, full MSI decode, exact SAPIEN payload recovery, supported installer arguments, VM selection, authorization, application acceptance, and rollback;
- guest isolation requirements: one package per clean snapshot, no host execution, disconnected or isolated-allowlist networking, no shared clipboard/folders, and AutoLogon excluded;
- skill, documentation, offline-runner, and Ubuntu/Windows package-analysis CI wiring;
- seven focused contract groups.

## Safety boundary

This PR does not start a VM, execute or copy a package, contact certificate or package endpoints, mutate a host or target, reboot a guest, perform rollback, authorize Allscripts, enable AutoLogon, or claim physical Cybernet acceptance. Runtime evidence remains operator-local and gitignored.

